cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal,
  work-in-progress synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI
  assistant by Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "ai-augmented-practice (work in progress)"
abstract: >-
  Every practice of the AI-augmented method read as an algorithm for a named problem: one page per practice with the problem class, the best-known algorithm and its reference implementation, the gap and the change proposed, in a table a program checks. Scope only; the review is not started.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/ai-augmented-practice"
license:
